Miki's

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.290
MARICI

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.290
SONTEN

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:16.790
Your secret is out!

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:18.120
You fooled us!

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.500
You and your not-fooling-anybody bald head!

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:20.250
Don't let the secret out!

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:20.250
You and your not-fooling-anybody bald head!

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.500
Don't let the secret out!

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:30.000
Panda Bridge

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.040
The snow...

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.540
It's all gone now.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.040
I wish it would snow every day.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.370
Colonel!

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.750
What are you doing out here?

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:44.120
Huh?

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.330
An acorn!

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.910
Did you bring this here, Colonel?

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.950
Kise Fruits

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.000
I'm glad you're here, Colors.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.700
There's been a robbery.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.410
A robbery?!

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.500
Sat-chan put a lucky cat statue here.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.040
It was here this morning, but now it's gone.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.500
You're right! It's gone!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.790
Did you do this, Colonel?

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.370
No, this isn't the Colonel's doing.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.040
How do I know?

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.370
The thief left a note, announcing their crime!

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:21.500
Alright! What a nice thief!

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.790
I've taken the lucky cat

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.410
I've taken the lucky cat.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.330
That's all?

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.410
Oh, and there's a scribble here.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.450
Sat-chan's Mom!

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.910
When did you last see the lucky cat?

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:38.040
Hmm, let me think.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.540
About three hours ago?

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.370
Three hours...

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.750
The perp might still be nearby!

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:46.000
Let's find them!

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.040
Okay! Operation: Find the Thief!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.580
Yeah!

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.620
There you go.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:58.080
You be the lucky cat until we find it, okay, Colonel?

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.080
Leader!

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.580
Adorable Sat-chan has an idea!

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.790
Yes, what is it, Average Sat-chan!

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:09.450
This case is a Level One.

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:11.660
So I think we should make it harder!

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:12.910
Harder?

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:17.200
From now until we solve the case,

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:17.200
I will only speak once.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.330
Just one time, when it's really important.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.580
What? That sounds like fun!

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:26.410
I'll prove that Sat-chan is cute

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:26.410
even when she doesn't say a word!

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:28.540
I wasn't really interested in that.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.040
Okay, we're starting now!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.330
Okay.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.040
Ready, begin!

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.620
Poop!

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.000
Poop!

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:39.450
Poop!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.000
Poop!

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.700
How about we just not solve this case?

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.370
Good idea.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.080
See you later!

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:53.910
Want some melon?

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:04.830
The only lucky cat I've got here is this one.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.330
Sat-chan, is this it?

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:12.750
Then I don't think I can help.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.370
Oh.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.750
Let's go look somewhere else!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.290
And search anyone who's carrying

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.290
a lucky cat with them.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:20.660
Yeah!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.370
See you later, Pops!

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:35.120
Sat-chan was awfully quiet.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.950
I don't see anyone carrying a lucky cat.

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:45.700
And no one's put any out in front of their shop, either.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:54.790
It's Saito-san!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.950
Should we ask him if he's seen anything?

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:05.450
We can't? Why not?

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.370
"Saito-san is..."

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:11.580
Um...

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:12.790
"...no good"?

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.370
"Lunchbox"?

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:18.950
"Dandelions..."

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.080
Put dandelions in his lunchbox?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.580
Huh? That's not right?

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.200
Then what is it?

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:33.500
I think she's saying we can't let him

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:33.500
see the note, or he'll take it away.

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:38.410
Oh, of course! You're so smart, Kotoha!

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.290
We'll just make sure he doesn't notice us.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.540
They're up to their weird tricks again.

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.910
Just ignore them... Just ignore them...

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:56.660
Nono-chan! Moka!

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.290
Oh, it's you!

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.250
Colors, yoo-hoo!

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.000
Where are you going?

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.580
Looking for ingredients for Nono's new product!

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:08.450
What? You mean that bread?

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:14.080
As a result of my tireless efforts,

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:14.080
it's tasting really good now.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.700
If you're interested, you should come by

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.700
and try it sometime.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.330
Okay. We probably won't, though.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:23.410
Good thinking. There's still

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:23.410
a lot of room for improvement.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:24.950
Maybe you should wait.

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:27.080
That's not true, okay?

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.290
It's yummy, okay?

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:31.950
Kaneno Naru Machi

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:31.790
What are you girls doing, Colors?

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:33.950
We're catching a thief!

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.330
What? A Thief?

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:36.910
Sounds rough.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.000
This is the note they left.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.700
What? Do you know something?

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.450
This is something my teacher told me.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.580
No one can understand another's feelings.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:00.250
Only the misperception that they do understand...

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:03.160
can ever approach the truth.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:06.080
Oh! There's still some snow!

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:10.120
You're awfully quiet today.

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:11.250
What's wrong?

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:15.370
Sat-chan said "poop," so now she can't talk.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:17.040
What does that mean?

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:18.790
I know!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.700
Let's say that if you use this acorn,

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.700
you can talk one more time.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.790
Use it wisely, okay?

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:30.160
Let's go have a strategy meeting at the hideout.

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:31.200
Indeed.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.580
See you later, Nono-chan, Moka!

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:35.580
Yeah! Bye-bye!

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:36.910
Buh-bye!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.200
It's a strange world they live in.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.160
Colors

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.200
Strategy meeting!

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.450
First.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.450
Judging from the crime itself, I can say one thing.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:54.660
The perp wants to put Kise Fruits out of business.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:57.370
No! Why?

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.580
They took the lucky cat.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:02.290
That means they don't want it attracting customers.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:04.290
I see.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:07.830
Sat-chan, did you do something to offend anyone?

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.330
Yeah. You do all the time.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.540
We have to solve this fast!

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:17.040
I've taken the lucky cat

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:18.080
I wonder if this scribble means anything.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:21.160
They might have just been testing a pen.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.870
That's true.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:23.950
Huh?

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.200
What's wrong?

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.450
There's some kind of powder on it.

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:31.040
Powder? Let me see that.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:39.910
I see. So that's how it is.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:42.000
Kotoha?

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.750
I know who the perp is.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:49.000
I've beat this game!

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:03.250
You little...!

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:08.750
You know that "I've beat this game"

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:08.750
is my all-important catchphrase!

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.040
Maybe I won't beat this game!

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.000
You'll never speak again!

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:17.160
Ugh, there you go, using the acorn

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:17.160
for something stupid.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:19.040
Don't call it stupid!

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:20.540
Alright.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.500
Say you're sorry and I'll forgive you.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.700
I'll beat this game...

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:26.620
if you say "sorry."

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:30.120
Oh, too bad. You can't say anything!

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.830
Never mind, just beat the game already, Kotoha!

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.290
Sasaki Bread

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:37.950
Yup, that's right.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.790
I'm the thief.

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.620
N..Nono-chan!

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:46.500
The powder on the perp's note was bread flour.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:49.620
Money

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:50.410
And it had a weird spicy smell.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:53.080
It's not a weird smell, it's a good smell!

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:57.660
You don't like Kise Fruits, Nono-chan?

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:57.660
You want them to go out of business?

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:00.200
What? Of course not!

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:01.750
Then why did you?

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:05.910
This is our lucky cat. I was just taking it back.

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.200
What? It's yours, Nono-chan?

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:12.450
Yeah. Sat-chan said she was

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:12.450
just going to borrow it for a day.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:14.500
But then she kept not giving it back.

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.700
Is that true, Sat-chan?

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.040
Ugh!

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:26.290
I've taken the lucky cat

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:26.330
And this wasn't supposed to announce a crime.

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:26.330
I was just leaving a note.

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.500
This scribble is my signature. It says Nono.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:30.750
Can't you tell?

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:32.700
Garbage.

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:36.370
Sat-chan. We solved the case, so you can talk again.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:39.750
Nonoka, I'm sorry!

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:42.160
That's just you, Sat-chan.

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.450
And Koto-chan, I'm sorry

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.450
for stealing your catchphrase!

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:46.750
If it happens again, I'm dumping you in the pond.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:53.830
Nonoka, do you get more customers with this here?

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:56.080
Not really.

00:20:57.200 --> 00:21:00.160
Oh! Want to try my new bread before you go?

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:01.370
No, I do not.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:03.000
Come on, sure you do!

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:03.790
Hey.

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.910
When I wasn't saying anything,

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.330
was I cute?

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:10.870
You were average.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.540
Kirari aizu wa ichiban-boshi

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.580
Otto sorosoro kaennakya

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:27.620
Otsu Colors

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.700
Otsu Colors

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:31.790
Kyou mo heiwa wa mamorareta

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:32.540
Yatta!

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.790
Wareware no kanzen shouri da!

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:38.950
Sanpochuu no chuu chuu kaburira

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.910
Kurae! Extra virgin oil!

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:44.750
Mainichi oo isogashi

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:47.080
Jiken level ichi kara doko made?

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.080
Donna nazo demo kaiketsu shichau yo

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:50.200
Game clear!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:51.120
Clear kita!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.080
Mata pinch no toki wa yobu to ii!

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:56.290
Kono machi no heiwa no tame ni!

00:21:56.450 --> 00:22:00.950
Orange no sora to yooi don shite

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:04.870
Issho ni ouchi e kaerou

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:09.080
Kitto ashita mo unto wakuwaku motto dekiru yo ne

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:11.910
Zen'in ajito dash de shuugou

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:17.160
Sayonara taiyou machi mo oyasumi

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:21.250
Ashita ga machidooshii na

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:25.290
Skip kokoro ga ukiuki tomaranai

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:29.620
Honjitsu mo ijou nashi!

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:32.200
Mata ashita

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:33.750
Mou ikkai

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:38.120
Mata ashita

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:44.330
There was a big thing today that needs improvement.

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:46.580
Ohh, Kotoha is being proactive today!

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:48.500
That's so weird! What happened?

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.330
It's gonna snow tomorrow!

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:52.080
Oh, I guess it already did!

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:55.040
Okay, Kotoha, go ahead!

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:58.290
Recently, the Colors have not been

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:58.290
solving enough mysteries.

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:01.870
Today I beat the game for the first time

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:01.870
since the center "ey".

00:23:01.870 --> 00:23:03.870
So we need more cases.

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:08.000
I didn't know you wanted to say

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:08.000
"I've beat this game" so badly today.

00:23:08.660 --> 00:23:11.040
Th-that's not necessarily what I'm going for.

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:13.910
I just realized something big!

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:15.200
What is it, Sat-chan?

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:18.040
If she hasn't said it in so long,

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:23.040
doesn't that mean "I've beat this game"

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:23.040
is not Koto-chan's catchphrase?

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:28.200
Wow, Sat-chan! That's a big discovery!

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:28.200
That's a very good point!

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.160
N-no, wait!

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:35.830
C-come to think of it, it hasn't been that long!

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:37.540
What? Really?

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:38.500
Really!

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:40.750
I say it every week in the ending sequence!
